# svc: what a service under /svc (ARCHITECTURE.md, "Userland": the
# namespace) may serve on its shared channel next to its own protocol: a
# channel of the caller's own, which speaks the service's protocol and
# goes when either end closes it. libos's svc_open calls it on a service
# whose namespace entry says it hands them out (<os.h>, "services"); a
# service that doesn't answers ERR_NOT_SUPPORTED, as for any other
# protocol's method. The music player does (user/services/music).
# Reconnect: a channel from connect sees ERR_PEER_CLOSED when the service
# ends; open the service again (svc_open), which calls connect on the
# shared channel the restarted service serves. A service that outlives
# its process (the mixer) keeps each connect's channel across its
# restarts instead: its clients see nothing.
# Format: see tools/genidl.py.

protocol svc 25

# A new channel to this service, for the caller alone.
# ERR_NO_RESOURCES: the service serves as many as it can.
1  connect  () -> (handle channel)
